{% comment %}
  How much stock a product may print a count for, one row per product.

  Every product shows "Only N left" once it is down to five units or fewer.
  A row here overrides that for one product and changes nothing else:

    threshold_handle   EasyStore product handle or SKU. Matched against the
                       product's handle, its SKU, and its variants' SKUs,
                       because a store exposes one or the other depending on how
                       the product was created. Case does not matter: the value
                       is normalized at runtime, so 'MTG-HOB-CBB-EN-PACK' and
                       'mtg-hob-cbb-en-pack' behave identically.
    threshold_maximum  the highest remaining count that still prints a notice,
                       or 'all' to print the count at every quantity. Delete the
                       row to put a product back on the shared default; handles
                       that are not listed here use that default.

  The first row that matches wins, so a specific SKU listed above a broader one
  keeps its own number. A row with a blank handle, a blank maximum, or a maximum
  that is neither a positive number nor 'all' is ignored rather than applied,
  which leaves the product on the default instead of hiding its notice.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  The default for every product that names no row of its own.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_threshold_default = 5 %}
{% comment %}
  The Hobbit Collector Booster pack sells its remaining stock as the draw, so it
  prints its count the whole way down instead of waiting for the last five.
{% endcomment %}
{% include 'low-inventory-threshold-row', threshold_handle: 'MTG-HOB-CBB-EN-PACK', threshold_maximum: 'all' %}
